# Committed default so index.html's %VITE_LICENSING_API_URL% CSP
# interpolation always has a defined (even if empty) value — without
# this, a plain `npm run build` run outside the Dockerfile's
# `VITE_LICENSING_API_URL="$VITE_LICENSING_API_URL" npm run build`
# wrapper leaves the literal, unsubstituted "%VITE_LICENSING_API_URL%"
# string in the shipped CSP header (Vite only interpolates html
# %VITE_*% placeholders it considers "defined"; merely unset doesn't
# count, an explicit empty value does). A real shell/Docker env var
# with the same name still overrides this at build time as usual.
VITE_LICENSING_API_URL=
